  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The best configuration so far is config_031 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) at 0.678 acc. The image-only resnet50 was very weak (0.208 acc), yet in multimodal it contributed ~3% over RNA-only scvi_n200 (0.650). The key uncertainty is whether the image modality's contribution is encoder-limited: resnet50 may be too coarse to capture relevant spatial/morphological features. Config_037 (scvi_n200 + ViT-L + avgpool + weighted) is a minimal, single-variable change from the best config, isolating the effect of a stronger image encoder. If ViT-L substantially improves over resnet50, it identifies a clear exploitation path; if not, it tells us the image signal is inherently limited and we should focus optimization on the RNA side. This is the highest-information experiment under the budget because it resolves a major design-axis uncertainty (image encoder quality) while building directly on the strongest evidence."
}

